CITIZEN PHEXT SKELETON — template only, provisioned per submitter by the backend at runtime. File name: citizen/<citizen_id>.phext. This skeleton contains placeholders in [brackets], never real data. Layout is specified in phexts/citizen-template.md and docs/COORDINATE-MAP.md.citizen_id: [cz-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX — opaque, server-derived]created_at: [RFC 3339 UTC — written once at provisioning]SUBMISSION LAYOUT — submission N (N from 1) lives in chapter 1+N. Within a submission chapter: section 1 = meta (tracking_code, form kind, submitted_at, content_hash), section 2 = one scroll per form field in form order, section 3 = status mirror (latest state copied from the claims register for the citizen's own view; register stays authoritative).tracking_code: [the code shown to the submitter]form: [ask-about-a-pilot]submitted_at: [RFC 3339 UTC]content_hash: [sha256 of field scrolls in coordinate order — same value as the claim's +3 scroll]field: program — [which suite program the citizen asks about]field: office — [office / agency name as given]field: need — [what the office needs, in the citizen's words]field: message — [free text as given]state: received